<title>UK: BTG up as licensee finishes clinical trials.</title>
<headline>BTG up as licensee finishes clinical trials.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in BTG Plc were up 45p to 1765p by 0844 GMT, after the company's licensee Genetics Institute completed clinical trials on a haemophilia treatment and filed a licence application with the U.S. Food and Drug Administration, traders said.  </p>
<p>The company said it also is seeking a new drug submission wih the Canadian Health Protection Branch, and a marketing authorization application with the European Medicines Evaluation agency for its recombinant Factor IX, a clotting factor used to treat Haemopholia B.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
